      speed.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"8795115f-c03d-4684-bf27-4e1b8d1a08f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8290.0,"yMin":96.0,"xMax":-8194.0,"yMax":160.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"48f42ed5-ff18-499e-8220-52e0c52da54c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3914.0,"yMin":-394.0,"xMax":-3724.0,"yMax":-305.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Make
      the player jump by adding the calculated jump force to Motion, then move the
      character with Motion.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"834ea1f1-48c3-4e15-bc28-a7227ac25f7c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4093.0,"yMin":-197.0,"xMax":-3956.0,"yMax":-116.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player can''t jump, check if they''re grounded.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"66af41e6-5c38-4c38-a27b-889ab05fbed7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7007.0,"yMin":5157.0,"xMax":-6869.0,"yMax":5239.0},"title":"Dash
      Cooldown","body":"This variable is controlled in the movement script.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"f573e478-acc2-43df-9265-db3590badb80","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7790.0,"yMin":-319.0,"xMax":-7694.0,"yMax":-255.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"82913233-80d9-4ee9-a89b-8ea4e3bc4b9e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5038.0,"yMin":2057.0,"xMax":-4883.0,"yMax":2136.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"Get a point that is a bit more than halfway down the player.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"e71c0329-35a1-44c5-80ad-d8bd94b1b079","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7031.0,"yMin":-820.0,"xMax":-6853.0,"yMax":-738.0},"title":"Movement","body":"This
      bit controls gravity, drag, and player walking and jumping.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"88859bb0-6601-40da-9ba7-50d08f832800","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6313.0,"yMin":3917.0,"xMax":-6182.0,"yMax":3994.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Makes
      the stick run relative to movement speed.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"3dee5e80-d03d-410e-a211-578162501c4a","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-9456.0,"yMin":849.0,"xMax":-9240.0,"yMax":942.0},"title":"Graveyard","body":"This
      long string is for if I ever want to try making dash defined as a distance
      instead of a force. For now, it is not worth it.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a08374f4-c50c-4647-b3df-971090c0899b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7576.0,"yMin":98.0,"xMax":-7480.0,"yMax":162.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"00d07eee-99d6-4e1c-8d67-09e323485f6c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4906.0,"yMin":6013.0,"xMax":-4539.0,"yMax":6104.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Turn
      off the animator so it isn''t trying to set the sprite, and manually set the
      sprite to the up-jumping one. If we make an animation for jumping and falling,
      this entire system will be redone, but my stolen sprites don''t have air animations.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"a5170fef-38a8-47d7-9878-ded7fe76e196","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8263.0,"yMin":-553.0,"xMax":-8126.0,"yMax":-489.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres/second","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"7ce45d6c-1f65-43ac-9ecf-b71d16e9404c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7960.0,"yMin":-548.0,"xMax":-7864.0,"yMax":-484.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"38a421d8-993f-4ff8-b99b-2cd18cdf02cb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2558.0,"yMin":-264.0,"xMax":-2345.667,"yMax":-172.5185},"title":"Movement","body":"Create
      the illusion of terminal velocity by clamping y velocity to a negative limit.
      The player can go up as fast as they want.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"9959c1a7-811f-460c-a142-6c00ba95de82","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8761.0,"yMin":-561.0,"xMax":-8638.0,"yMax":-441.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"Activate
      all the object variables for consistency across scenes. I have noted all their
      units.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"eb80ec44-2936-4296-a9c7-fd7d8d8111c9","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8515.0,"yMin":333.0,"xMax":-8419.0,"yMax":397.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"c2d710dd-2947-48e2-93f7-169b7caffd5e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4091.0,"yMin":5788.0,"xMax":-3972.0,"yMax":5877.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Do
      the same thing with the down-jumping sprite.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"31c0d722-45e7-4422-8bc7-f4cadc917967","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4305.0,"yMin":1296.0,"xMax":-4148.0,"yMax":1361.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Move
      the player with that calculated force.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"cbe3a90b-dc1e-4da6-83c7-1cf2bc14b022","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5274.0,"yMin":-250.0,"xMax":-5085.333,"yMax":-141.0},"title":"Movement","body":"The
      Motion variable is what eventually gets used to move the player. First, it
      is set to the accelerating movement input.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a94951ba-ecbe-47d5-967a-037061522762","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4311.0,"yMin":3988.0,"xMax":-4169.0,"yMax":4065.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"If
      the animator is turned off (if we are jumping) turn it on.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"c7ea0431-03ee-4ef2-b2f4-3f71c4df431d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5719.0,"yMin":-19.0,"xMax":-5492.667,"yMax":88.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is giving an input, store the direction of that input. 1 is right
      and -1 is left, respective to the camera. If the player is not giving an input,
      set it to 0.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"48b5968f-e3d3-4bdb-b0b1-261afe5e9ba9","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7582.0,"yMin":324.0,"xMax":-7445.0,"yMax":388.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres/second","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"b0585c79-f766-4924-8a8f-dc113e38de4f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4310.0,"yMin":1902.0,"xMax":-4084.0,"yMax":2016.667},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds something, the player is grounded, so stops
      accelerating downwards, turns off the fastfall toggle, and regains all their
      jumps and dashes.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"1534c3c1-4511-40b9-85b8-a540a687e69b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6467.0,"yMin":32.0,"xMax":-6285.0,"yMax":136.0},"title":"Display
      MaxSpeed","body":"This calculates the max speed of the player based on drag
      and acceleration speed. It is \"displayed\" as an object variable.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"7114167e-fbc2-4585-a9bf-7f5a5cc91fb7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4679.0,"yMin":1998.0,"xMax":-4484.0,"yMax":2107.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"This lovely node checks if there is anything within the box
      just defined. The Layer Mask means anything not in that layer will be ignored.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"b0759b95-1179-414c-bd47-3ea7a7dd0c0e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5261.0,"yMin":-1322.0,"xMax":-5053.667,"yMax":-1230.0},"title":"Z-Lock","body":"Stop
      the player from falling off the front or back of the map by constantly setting
      its Z position to 0, the centre of the world.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c13976e4-772e-45cc-8886-b21e34101c69","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5541.0,"yMin":-745.0,"xMax":-5351.0,"yMax":-678.0},"title":"Input
      Scale","body":"Add the current velocity in units/timestep to accelerate.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"1e93d8ec-48de-4e41-9571-e54275bd4663","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3436.0,"yMin":-114.0,"xMax":-3336.0,"yMax":-24.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is grounded, don''t move downwards.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"e6ef0479-c3b9-4c19-a9a5-8272e6017139","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4488.0,"yMin":-824.0,"xMax":-4213.0,"yMax":-701.0},"title":"Jump
      Height","body":"To make the player jump a consistent height in m no matter
      what the gravity is.\nThe formula is yVelocity = sqrt(JumpHeight x gravity
      x -2), but there''s a delta time in there because Unity measures most things
      in m/s not timestep.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"2a859ead-85a4-4a70-a75d-40e78d630db7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6472.0,"yMin":2359.0,"xMax":-6290.0,"yMax":2449.0},"title":"Inputs","body":"Fastfall
      is effectively a toggle, it turns off once the player hits the ground, the
      player can''t turn it off.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"b20b1bbc-955c-40d5-bd90-b432d886082e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7808.0,"yMin":100.0,"xMax":-7712.0,"yMax":164.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"a8062e97-2d9b-4aac-8ae0-e927d8e21f14","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8042.0,"yMin":94.0,"xMax":-7946.0,"yMax":158.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"9d3eceb4-b300-45d6-91ba-e2502a06c559","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8173.0,"yMin":4358.0,"xMax":-8014.0,"yMax":4454.0},"title":"Hurt","body":"Triggered
      by things that deal damage. Just changes health by the given damage.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c5411e3b-0936-4e21-a32e-923df96d7f08","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3381.0,"yMin":351.0,"xMax":-3190.0,"yMax":432.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is not grounded, accelerate them towards the ground.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"91df67b4-f70a-4dec-b0b7-fb7151e53936","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3638.0,"yMin":5849.0,"xMax":-3469.0,"yMax":5940.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Otherwise,
      (if the player is on the ground) turn the animator back on if it isn''t already.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"6fe0b18c-10c2-458b-9aa0-99f1dcd97e74","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6005.0,"yMin":4302.0,"xMax":-5816.333,"yMax":4406.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Scale
      the animation speed by velocity times something small. This will need tweaking
      when we have proper animations.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"59197339-53f9-4d25-97aa-b3d91e8ec907","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7385.0,"yMin":4788.0,"xMax":-7259.0,"yMax":4882.0},"title":"Health
      Bar","body":"Get the child at position 3 (index 2) which is the health bar.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"3f7c22f2-7f11-4a66-8c61-f679a60ce6bb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7816.0,"yMin":2438.0,"xMax":-7632.0,"yMax":2503.0},"title":"Inputs","body":"There
      is a   space   in this box. Please don''t touch it.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"56246ae2-f6ed-47ca-afdc-da0c477ef435","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8139.0,"yMin":4765.0,"xMax":-7981.0,"yMax":4859.0},"title":"UI
      Display","body":"Controls the UI elements of the player. Currently, health
      bar and dash cooldown.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"b64987ad-401b-4e97-b4ad-3a6de88d3b48","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4110.0,"yMin":1588.0,"xMax":-3972.0,"yMax":1676.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Add
      a count to the number of dashes and turn off the button input press.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"38657199-a64d-4e77-b97b-7f7a3ee42606","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4920.0,"yMin":3426.0,"xMax":-4757.0,"yMax":3545.0},"title":"Attack
      Animations","body":"This system is very temporary. It only animates, it doesn''t
      do any attacking. If it makes it into a commit, don''t touch it.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"c88670b4-dd92-404f-a2ac-60dfe3f04837","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4323.333,"yMin":2331.0,"xMax":-4131.0,"yMax":2436.333},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds nothing, the player is not grounded. It is
      still called GravityGrounded from an older version of the jump system.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"be2bcd56-207e-466f-abbe-24ae8351dcbb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5343.0,"yMin":3943.0,"xMax":-5128.0,"yMax":4048.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Tell
      the animator if the player is moving. The animator doesn''t actually care which
      way they are moving, it just cares whether they are or not.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"b27d58c0-7ee0-4893-889a-5edfcad28ab4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-1558.0,"yMin":-105.0,"xMax":-1423.0,"yMax":-30.0},"title":"Movement","body":"After
      all that, move the player with the calculated speed.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"9e86260b-d9b7-4cbf-9478-cc10c84f82ef","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8561.0,"yMin":96.0,"xMax":-8465.0,"yMax":160.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"642ae9cb-aea9-467c-beec-49ee2d3dadd8","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7618.0,"yMin":4783.0,"xMax":-7437.0,"yMax":4876.0},"title":"Player
      Display","body":"Get the Canvas that has all the UI elements on it. Hardcoded
      indices are bad practice but I am lazy.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"74adc13d-d37c-47b9-aea6-cd5dd53b8253","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3514.0,"yMin":-508.0,"xMax":-3350.0,"yMax":-428.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Add
      a count to the number of jumps and turn off the jump button.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"94bf0010-fe68-4eed-9c8c-b064660906f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4427.0,"yMin":-270.0,"xMax":-4289.0,"yMax":-177.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is pressing Jump and they haven''t used all their jumps...","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"33222291-ee51-4967-97e4-bbfecbb0635e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8446.0,"yMin":3232.0,"xMax":-8295.0,"yMax":3296.0},"title":"Visuals","body":"This
      half controls the UI and animations.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"f08138f1-344e-447d-b196-a8a77e067be7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4808.0,"yMin":4451.0,"xMax":-4588.0,"yMax":4605.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"If
      we are not currently animating an attack, check if any attack inputs are pressed,
      and which one. The convenient Switch node selects a flow based on the current
      input. These systems are basically identical, so I will only comment the top
      one.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"a45df6b3-b856-4cf3-be6f-decde6a613b0","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7899.0,"yMin":5031.0,"xMax":-7782.0,"yMax":5124.0},"title":"Health
      Bar","body":"Store the current amount of health as a float from 0-1.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"c13e46a3-f180-49fa-9a13-4dd53d897dc3","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8544.0,"yMin":-555.0,"xMax":-8407.0,"yMax":-491.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres/second","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"4f8205a5-f77f-4b0b-a668-10ae44434515","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7505.0,"yMin":-547.0,"xMax":-7368.0,"yMax":-483.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"honestly,
      not sure. probably m/s?","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"1d6d829e-a05b-4cf9-aebe-ed4fa2db4972","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2185.0,"yMin":159.0,"xMax":-2031.0,"yMax":223.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Then
      apply drag to the movement input.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"dbc73ccf-db8a-454a-86f0-fe7a98bdc10e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5378.0,"yMin":4382.0,"xMax":-5114.0,"yMax":4517.0},"title":"Moving","body":"If
      the player has velocity but isn''t pushing an input, they will animate idle.
      This makes them animate idle while moving for a moment, but it isn''t very
      noticeable and is better than the alternative, animating very slowly as the
      character stops from drag.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"63df4471-6bae-4c27-8cd8-d082ef7cca27","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2591.0,"yMin":4206.0,"xMax":-2480.0,"yMax":4283.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Wait
      until the animation is finished.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"baae3409-5dab-4990-8233-d9a1293f429c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8749.0,"yMin":1367.0,"xMax":-8599.0,"yMax":1459.0},"title":"Inputs","body":"Tells
      the graph when the player is trying to jump, dash, fastfall or attack.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"95b35221-73b6-46f2-aeb9-91ac3ffda104","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3526.0,"yMin":1250.0,"xMax":-3282.333,"yMax":1360.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Run
      a cooldown for the defined amount of time. While it runs, update the cooldown
      percent variable for the indicator. Once it finishes, allow the player to dash
      again.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"2b046fea-6238-4d9e-88ce-befcaf137d75","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5717.0,"yMin":3951.0,"xMax":-5514.0,"yMax":4042.0},"title":"Moving","body":"If
      the player is moving, tell the animator that. The animator multiplies the animation
      speed by this value.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"64128d06-def1-4d34-85da-63a4b3cc3687","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2868.0,"yMin":157.0,"xMax":-2519.667,"yMax":251.0},"title":"Drag","body":"Calculates
      drag.\nThe formula is velocity / ( 1 + Drag ), with a delta time because Unity
      stores everything in m/s not timestep. Y drag never worked out properly, so
      it is disconnected.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"474c5565-6804-4b2d-8e90-dbf8b51c71d4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4460.0,"yMin":5806.0,"xMax":-4354.0,"yMax":5885.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"If
      the player''s y velocity is negative...","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"41c21d1e-9cfc-494a-ad47-3616ff0b615f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4515.0,"yMin":1108.0,"xMax":-4197.0,"yMax":1232.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Calculate
      how far the player will dash by multiplying the distance by direction (positive
      for right, negative for left, 0 goes nowhere). Then add that to the velocity
      in m/timestep. If the player isn''t giving an input or the character isn''t
      moving, dashing consumes a charge but does nothing.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"04830f34-b424-4a5f-aa67-b0cad8b7dae4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3788.0,"yMin":149.0,"xMax":-3615.0,"yMax":227.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player wants to fast fall, set their velocity instantly to terminal.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"bb915bd9-4289-4f01-bd6c-3cd1a918b1bf","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8282.0,"yMin":330.0,"xMax":-8186.0,"yMax":394.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"f86aedda-1679-403c-8552-d2fb29acc68e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8399.0,"yMin":-332.0,"xMax":-8303.0,"yMax":-268.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"fdf2a9fa-ff55-45e2-a5d1-b510a85e1747","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4664.0,"yMin":177.0,"xMax":-4419.0,"yMax":287.0},"title":"Gravity","body":"When
      the player isn''t on the ground, they should accelerate towards it. To do this,
      get the current velocity and the constant gravity, make them into m/timestep,
      and add them up.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"d31392d4-e184-4235-acaf-da82c29901dc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6401.0,"yMin":3414.0,"xMax":-6247.667,"yMax":3507.0},"title":"Animations","body":"This
      big flow is for animating the player (or currently the stick), every frame.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"51ade278-49d8-46ca-8397-873fd1af7490","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8784.0,"yMin":-1334.0,"xMax":-8606.0,"yMax":-1252.0},"title":"Object","body":"This
